    {
      "id": "HNUG1e5milhcu4vncJNzn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2808.666666666667,
      "y": -61.3333333333328,
      "width": 508.61126708984375,
      "height": 65,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBs",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1882634152,
      "version": 252,
      "versionNonce": 1761671336,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782859412143,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- It reads the FED, not the MARKET. To trade the dollar we still need a 'what is already\n  priced in' layer (futures / OIS / the rate path) to compare against, plus a step that\n  turns the surprise into an actual dollar move. This paper gives us the Fed-reading and\n  surprise half; we must build the market-expectation and price-reaction half. [us]",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- It reads the FED, not the MARKET. To trade the dollar we still need a 'what is already\n  priced in' layer (futures / OIS / the rate path) to compare against, plus a step that\n  turns the surprise into an actual dollar move. This paper gives us the Fed-reading and\n  surprise half; we must build the market-expectation and price-reaction half. [us]",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0HChzSUbw8jiyS5uoTj4O",
